{:edb/db-before-t 2742 :edb/db-after-t 2743 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536055 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:54:35.590Z" 13194139536055 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381201 13194139536055 true] [17592186100802 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381215 13194139536055 true] [17592186100803 1020 #edb/ref 17592186381208 13194139536055 true] [17592186381201 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381202 13194139536055 true] [17592186381201 1089 "q-102668" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381201 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536055 true] [17592186381201 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{t-5}{2},\\,\\,\\,y=({t}^{2}-25)(t-4),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381201 1113 #uuid "f662300f-f189-53c3-b854-815e04ddab5a" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381201 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{t-5}{2}\\,⇒\\,t=2x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=2x+5$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =((2x+5)^{2}-25)(2x+5-4) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+20x+25-25)(2x+1) \\\\  & =(4{x}^{2}+20x)(2x+1) \\\\  & =4x(x+5)(2x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=4x(x+5)(2x+1).$" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381203 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381204 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381205 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381206 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381207 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1041 "selection" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381207 13194139536055 true] [17592186381202 1110 #uuid "e83a50a6-01bf-5730-9930-1af38c0fb461" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381203 1034 "y=(2x+1)^{3}" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381203 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381203 1111 #uuid "ab374465-0f5d-5ef1-ac40-b3e35c2ef8a1" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381204 1034 "y=2x(x-5)(2x+1)" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381204 1111 #uuid "158970c7-5b1d-57f4-9b6a-03b6ca1ae2cc" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381205 1034 "y=4x(2x+1)(2x-5)" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381205 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381205 1111 #uuid "b65139e2-0c50-5423-b3a0-6c9691d0733a" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381206 1034 "y=2(2x+1)^{3}" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381206 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381206 1111 #uuid "da9cd34f-c2ab-518b-8132-46abdb181301" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381207 1034 "y=4x(x+5)(2x+1)" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381207 1111 #uuid "a2e14081-8b1c-529e-ae73-129b8cac5b07" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381208 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381209 13194139536055 true] [17592186381208 1089 "q-24378" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381208 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536055 true] [17592186381208 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381208 1113 #uuid "615bfb39-f4dc-5e2d-9395-b7631c9499f8" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381208 1145 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using double angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =(1-{sin}^{2}⁡t)-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3} & =1-2{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}).$" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381210 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381211 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381212 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381213 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381214 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1041 "selection" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381214 13194139536055 true] [17592186381209 1110 #uuid "a92445cb-46d5-5049-82b6-6f64444df8e7" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381210 1034 "y=2(1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381210 1111 #uuid "19c9a8c6-e009-53b4-b12c-0191de7a91a0" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381211 1034 "y=3(1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381211 1111 #uuid "f5ab26b6-08da-5425-8654-994a301549cf" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381212 1034 "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381212 1111 #uuid "dc5f842c-bee5-53ec-b816-9d6d014e513f" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381213 1034 "y=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381213 1111 #uuid "85c9a6ce-7931-5053-8f42-5a2270259829" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381214 1034 "y=3(1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381214 1111 #uuid "876b5dc7-1fb2-5f36-929d-970b1e677209" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381215 1017 #edb/ref 17592186381216 13194139536055 true] [17592186381215 1089 "q-321084" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381215 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536055 true] [17592186381215 1100 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\,t+1\\,},\\,\\,\\,y=t(4-t),\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,x\\ge 1.$" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381215 1113 #uuid "9c4b3f61-cafc-57f5-8068-37339299eacb" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381215 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{\\,t+1\\,}\\,⇒\\,t={x}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t={x}^{2}-1$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =({x}^{2}-1)(4-({x}^{2}-1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-1)(5-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=({x}^{2}-1)(5-{x}^{2}).$\n\nFinally, since $t\\ge 0$ and $t={x}^{2}-1,$ we must have ${x}^{2}-1\\ge 0,$ i.e., $x\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the complete Cartesian equation is $y=({x}^{2}-1)(5-{x}^{2}),\\,x\\ge 1.$" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381216 1000 #edb/ref 17592186381217 13194139536055 true] [17592186381216 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536055 true] [17592186381216 1041 "field-1" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381216 1104 #edb/ref 17592186381217 13194139536055 true] [17592186381216 1110 #uuid "efc94e2d-73ec-5487-af0a-0d200a851b62" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381217 1034 "-x^4+6x^2-5" 13194139536055 true] [17592186381217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536055 true] [17592186381217 1111 #uuid "0b02216e-1888-53d2-a339-64d43470e022" 13194139536055 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-102668" 17592186381201 "q-102668/selection" 17592186381202 "q-102668/selection/0860209cab1584dd19ee00be7d98cc074c05ab9705a55f5c6eaedfbe9c97f2f6" 17592186381203 "q-